        "original_id": "3fdc65fc-27ed-5a75-a1d6-06789ad2a7c0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Elaine Duke, John F. Kelly, Donald Trump\n- Roles: Acting United States Secretary of Homeland Security, United States Deputy Secretary of Homeland Security, White House Chief of Staff, United States Secretary of Homeland Security\n- Organizations: United States Department of Homeland Security, White House\n\nFacts:\n- Elaine Duke, born in 1958, is an American civil servant.\n- John F. Kelly was born on May 11, 1950.\n- On January 30, 2017, President Donald Trump nominated Elaine Duke to become United States Deputy Secretary of Homeland Security under John F. Kelly.\n- John F. Kelly previously served as United States Secretary of Homeland Security in the Trump administration.\n- On July 31, 2017, John F. Kelly became White House Chief of Staff for President Donald Trump.\n- On July 31, 2017, Elaine Duke became Acting United States Secretary of Homeland Security when John F. Kelly assumed the office of White House Chief of Staff.\n- Elaine Duke is the current Acting United States Secretary of Homeland Security.\n- John F. Kelly is the current White House Chief of Staff for President Donald Trump.",
